KZ3 patch 2033: cheaper texture change detection and the vertex-fetch profile (pass 34).

- ld_fast_hash: the per-frame texture content hash (and the vertex-texture hash) runs four
  independent lanes instead of one FNV chain; same bytes in, mutation detection only.
- LD_TEX_HASH_SPAN=N (default 0 = off): a cached texture whose hash was unchanged N times in a
  row is re-hashed every N frames unless a tracked writer touched its span. Tracked writers mark
  a 64 KB page bitmap per location: the walker's own stores (NV0039 copies, NV3089 blits, NV308A
  inline writes, surface write-backs) and SPU DMA puts (spu_dma.h -> cellGcm_note_guest_write_ea
  through a hook pointer in spu_coherency.c that cellGcmInit installs via a weak function reference). Direct PPU stores are not tracked;
  [tex-hash] counts hash changes that no tracked write preceded ("untracked").
- [perf-vtx]: the vertex-fetch split (refs, remap, fetch, copy) and volumes inside the
  RSX_PERF_PROF window; rsx_vertex_decode_fast hoists the type switch out of the component loop;
  rsx_vertex_remap_build takes a dense id range as the unique list instead of the hash table.
- Texture cache: MAX_TEXTURES 1024 -> 8192 (the level binds ~2,500 distinct textures a frame and the LRU
  evicted ~243 per frame, each decoded again; RE pass 72) with a hash-indexed lookup in place of the
  linear scan per bind.

Rebased on ps3recomp v0.15.0 (SPU pass 81): context only, upstream engine-wrote note added next to ours, both kept.

Rebased on ps3recomp v0.18.0 (SPU pass 108): decode_fast moved to upstream's rsx_vertex_fetch_attr_value (single-vertex path); upstream's attribute-major fetch_many left as is.

